# Frontend

This is a student PWA used mostly on a phone. Desktop can look good, but mobile is the default.

## Pages

- Logged out: `/` landing and `/login`. No dashboard sidebar.
- Logged in: `/app` with 5 hash-routed views: Home, Attendance (Subjects / Calendar), Results, Materials (ETLab / Saved links), Settings. Routes look like `#attendance/calendar/2026-09-09`.
- Landing navbar is logo + Log in. Already signed in users skip landing and go to `/app`.
- Settings is account/sync/install, not a login form.

## Layout

- Phone app chrome: bottom tab bar, not a sticky dark sidebar that turns into a horizontal scroller.
- Respect safe-area insets. Main content must not hide under the tab bar.
- Touch targets at least 44px. Primary actions stay visible without hunting.

## Visual language

Premium and minimal: warm paper/ink neutrals, one clay accent, lots of space, hairlines instead of boxes.

- Design tokens live at the top of `base.css` (`--bg`, `--panel`, `--panel-soft`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--faint`, `--line`, `--line-strong`, `--brand`, `--ink`, `--on-ink`, `--danger`), with a `:root[data-theme="dark"]` override. Reuse them; do not invent a second palette. `base.css` also holds type, buttons, form fields and motion; `public.css` is landing/login only; `app.css` is the signed-in app.
- Status colour is three states only, via `data-tone`: `safe` (ink), `close` (within 5 points of the target, `--brand`), `risk` (below target, `--danger`). No green-to-red ramps.
- Fonts: Instrument Serif for display headings (italic `em` in `--brand` for the accent word), Geist for UI text, Geist Mono for small uppercase labels and numbers.
- Themes: light and dark. The inline `<head>` script sets `data-theme` before paint (stored in `localStorage["better-etlab-theme"]`, else the OS setting); `ui.js` handles the toggle.
- Primary buttons are ink pills (`.btn-primary`); secondary are hairline ghost pills. The accent is for emphasis only, not for large fills.
- Motion: short eased entrances (`.rise`, headline `.w` words, `[data-reveal]` on scroll), hover effects only under `@media (hover: hover)`, and everything must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

Avoid AI-slop defaults:

- Decorative "good / warn / bad" pills as the main UI
- Card-in-card layouts, heavy drop shadows, big radius on everything
- Purple gradients, glassmorphism, blobs, fake empty-state illustrations
- 7-column calendars that overflow on a 360px screen

## Content density

- Landing stays short: what it is, what you get, one login action.
- Dashboard should answer "am I in trouble?" in one screen, then get out of the way.
- Attendance calendar must be usable on a phone: compact cells or a list/week switch, not tiny unreadable day cards.
- Lists (materials, results) should scan: title, subject, one action. No nested card-in-card.

## How to change UI

Edit the matching page files (`index.html`, `login.html`, `app.html`, `base.css`, `public.css`, `app.css`, and the JS for that page). New static files must also be added to `STATIC_FILES` in `backend_server.py` and `APP_SHELL` in `sw.js`. Prefer CSS and markup changes over new JS frameworks.
